======================================================================
SUMMARY: Is Norm Causally Related to Position Encoding?
======================================================================

Key Findings:

1. NORM EQUALIZATION:
   - Baseline R²: 0.0650
   - After equalization (same probe) R²: 0.1011
   - R² drop: -0.0361 (-55.6% relative)
   - Retrained on equalized R²: 0.7504
   
2. NORM SWAPPING:
   - Correlation with original position: 0.4983
   - Correlation with swapped position: -0.4983
   - Predictions follow: ORIGINAL POSITION

3. NORM-ONLY DECODING (post_attn_residual layer):
   - Full activations R²: 0.0381
   - Norm only R²: 0.4937
   - Direction only R²: 0.7551

CONCLUSION:

  ✗ Norm equalization has little effect → Norm alone is not sufficient
  ✗ Predictions don't follow norms → Direction also matters
  ✓ Norm alone achieves most of full R² → Norm is PRIMARY mechanism
